  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "One or two given names and a family name, usually inherited from the father, though couples may keep either name or join them with a hyphen. Most German family names come from trades (Müller, Schmidt, Fischer) or places. Turkish German families keep Turkish names, often written without the Turkish letters on German documents (Yilmaz for Yılmaz). Families from Poland, the former Soviet Union, the Arab world, the Balkans, Italy and Vietnam keep their own names; many Russian German Aussiedler carry old German surnames like Klassen or Friesen.",
